  "narrative": "The newly delivered deadline validation resolves the two original claims without changing the central scientific picture. For H25, feature_010 = 1 versus 0 within feature_036 <= 0, discovery R24 gave a signed mean difference of +0.799 composite dependency-score units (lower +0.716), and independent validation R39 gave +0.826 with independent lower bound +0.693. That lower bound is far above the +0.15 threshold, so I reassess and confirm H25 as accepted and closed. For H29, the original hypothesis was that feature_037 = 1 versus 0 is positively associated with higher outcome_001, but the signed evidence is strongly negative. Discovery R29 was -0.804 with interval -0.866 to -0.742, and independent validation R38 was -0.827 with interval -0.923 to -0.731. The validation therefore supports the opposite direction, which is already captured by the reversed claim H50: feature_037 = 1 is associated with lower outcome_001, meaning stronger composite dependency. Accordingly, H29 remains rejected and closed, while H50 remains accepted and closed. These deadline assessments also reinforce the core supported dataset-level associations: feature_010 = 1 and feature_002 = 1 are each associated with higher outcome_001, meaning weaker dependency, while feature_037 = 1 is associated with lower outcome_001, meaning stronger dependency. All three validated effects are large, roughly 0.74 to 0.83 composite dependency-score units, and all are well beyond the 0.15 threshold. Pairwise conditional analyses show each core association persists when conditioning on one other core predictor, usually with signed lower bounds above +0.65, so they are not simple one-marker proxies in this dataset. However, the interaction screen among the three core predictors is not meaningful at the threshold: signed interaction point estimates were only about 0.02 to 0.08, H59, H60, and H62 are rejected, and H61, H75, and H76 remain unresolved in status but I close their investigations because validation would not plausibly convert point estimates far below 0.15 into threshold-level effects. The registered marker/signature interaction screens are similarly non-promising and are closed as unresolved or rejected according to their evidence. Categorical screens are mostly negative: feature_046 level_002 versus level_001 is statistically positive but its upper bound is below the +0.15 scientific threshold, so it is rejected; feature_046 level_003 versus level_001 is too uncertain to accept; feature_059 level_001 versus level_003 and feature_054 contrasts are null or opposite to the claimed direction; sparse feature_059 level_002 versus level_003 is too unstable to support. Remaining uncertainty is important: all claims are observational associations in the supplied dataset, not causal effects, not biological mechanism, and not generalizable claims. The pairwise conditional contrasts and near-marginal independence are informative but still do not constitute joint adjustment for latent confounding or all latent structure. The most informative next analysis is a joint-stratum refinement: test each core binary association within the reference joint cell defined by the other two predictors, using feature_002 = 0 and feature_037 = 0 for feature_010, feature_010 = 0 and feature_037 = 0 for feature_002, and feature_010 = 0 and feature_002 = 0 for feature_037. If these three contrasts remain large and threshold-level, the additive dataset-level interpretation is further strengthened; if any attenuates materially, that would identify a joint-stratum dependency worth localization and validation.",
  "research_notes": "Final synthesis after Phase 5 validation: accepted validated core dataset-level associations are H13 feature_010=1 higher outcome_001, H26 feature_002=1 higher outcome_001, and H50 feature_037=1 lower outcome_001. Deadline validation H25 accepted (feature_010 association persists in feature_036<=0 stratum; validation lower +0.693); H29 remains rejected because the original positive feature_037 claim is opposite to discovery and validation evidence. Pairwise interactions among feature_010/002/037 are not threshold-level: H59/H60/H62 rejected; H61/H75/H76 closed unresolved because signed point estimates are only 0.02-0.08 and validation is not informative. Categorical screen: H67 rejected below threshold; H68 unresolved closed as uncertain below threshold; H69 rejected; H70 unresolved closed as sparse/null; H77/H78 rejected. Marker/signature interactions H9/H10/H18/H19 closed unresolved; H1/H2/H3/H7/H8/H11/H12 reject main effects/interactions. Core interpretation: three robust, separately validated, pairwise-persistent associations, approximately additive within measured strata, but observational and not causal. Next priority registered: joint-stratum mean differences for feature_010 in feature_002=0 & feature_037=0; feature_002 in feature_010=0 & feature_037=0; feature_037 in feature_010=0 & feature_002=0. Remaining untested broad binary/categorical screens lower priority."
